From 932d5c6ca47d17b82fc58c91d65c7c17bcc142bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:05:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add raw-signal queue: score cheap/free signals before
 spending Clay credits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduces a separate raw_signals table + /api/raw-signals/ingest endpoint
that accepts pre-enrichment signal hits (from scripts/signal-sources/, or
any other cheap source), applies a transparent rule-based score
(signal type weight + recency + already-has-a-contact + verifiable
source), and auto-marks anything clearing RAW_SIGNAL_QUALIFY_THRESHOLD
(default 50) as "qualified" while leaving the rest for manual triage.

Adds a "Raw signals" tab to the review UI (basicAuth-protected, same as
the existing Sequences queue) to see the queue, filter by status, and
qualify/dismiss with a reviewer note.

The idea: Clay currently does both "find the trigger" and "find/enrich
the contact" and charges credits for both on every row. This slice lets
cheap/free sources (Companies House scan, job-board scan, etc.) handle
trigger-finding, so Clay only spends credits enriching contacts for
signals a human or the score has already decided are worth it.

Does NOT yet include the Clay hand-off endpoint (Clay polling this app
for qualified signals) — full design and the reasoning for deferring it
(retry/ack semantics need a real decision) is in
docs/raw-signal-pipeline.md.

Also updates the Companies House scraper script to post into the new
raw-signal queue instead of straight to /api/ingest, since it has no
verified contact email yet.

